Here is the complete, correct sequence to type inside virt-rescue, using the real values from your clone (disk /dev/sda, LVM on sda5, VG vglocalhost, swap UUID from your blkid).

Before opening virt-rescue (host)
sudo virsh destroy auto-ranv3Node1
sudo qemu-img info -U /mnt/SSD/auto-ranv3Node1.qcow2
sudo virt-rescue -a /mnt/SSD/auto-ranv3Node1.qcow2

Confirm there is no backing file: line, and that you opened the clone’s file, not the base.

Inside virt-rescue (the ><rescue> prompt)

1. Check the layout

vgchange -ay
lvs
parted /dev/sda unit GiB print
blkid /dev/vglocalhost/swap_1

Expect sda5 (lvm) starting at 0.50GiB, root ~264g, swap_1 976m, swap UUID c2e6f0a0-1ba0-4e68-bdad-0037f1b24da2.

2. Remove swap (answer y)

lvremove /dev/vglocalhost/swap_1

3. Check the filesystem, then shrink root and its filesystem together

e2fsck -f /dev/vglocalhost/root
lvreduce -r -L 40G /dev/vglocalhost/root

If e2fsck asks to fix free-count mismatches, answer y.

4. Shrink the physical volume (answer y)

pvresize --setphysicalvolumesize 46G /dev/sda5

5. Shrink the partitions (logical sda5 first, then the extended sda2; answer Yes to any warning)

parted /dev/sda resizepart 5 48GiB
parted /dev/sda resizepart 2 48GiB

6. Recreate swap with the original UUID

lvcreate -L 976M -n swap_1 vglocalhost
mkswap -U c2e6f0a0-1ba0-4e68-bdad-0037f1b24da2 /dev/vglocalhost/swap_1

7. Verify before leaving

vgs; lvs
parted /dev/sda unit GiB print

You should see:

vgs: VG under 46G
lvs: root 40G, swap_1 976M
parted: sda2 and sda5 both ending at 48.0GiB

8. Leave the shell

exit
Back on the host (last step)
sudo qemu-img resize --shrink /mnt/SSD/auto-ranv3Node1.qcow2 50G
sudo qemu-img info -U /mnt/SSD/auto-ranv3Node1.qcow2
sudo virsh start auto-ranv3Node1

Virtual size should show 50 GiB.

Verify inside the VM
df -h /
lsblk
free -h

Expect root about 39G, vda 50G, swap 976M.

Notes
Your earlier session already did steps 2 to 6 on this clone. If you are continuing from that, go straight to step 7, then exit, then the host commands.
Do not run qemu-img resize --shrink until parted shows both partitions ending at 48.0GiB.
The “cannot find name for group ID 0” line when virt-rescue starts is harmless.





